    I was born in Tan Phung, a small fishing town in My Tho, Phu My, Binh Dinh
along the long coastline that stretches toward Quy Nhon City.
My childhood was shaped by the sea, sand, and the rhythm of fishing life

    One of my strongest memories is eating fly fish roe taken straight from
the nets on the beach - a simple joyful moment that only someone raise in a
fish village would know

   After 60 years Now living in California I finally returned to my hometown
Standing there again brought a powerful mix of motions;
  Peace, because I was there;
  Gratitude, because I could return after so long;
  Sadness, because so much had changed;
  and Hope, because my memories were still alive
